Q: How do I remove the variables in an element of an array across 2 classes? A: <p>Your <code>removalId</code> is scoped to the <code>if</code>  block, so its gone on the next line. declare it before the loop with a sentinel. And squadSize is a primitive copy, decrementing it here doesnt affect the caller, so return the new size instead.</p>
<p>Dont just null the slot either, that leaves a hole and later loops will NPE on <code>players[i].name</code>. shift the tail down.</p>
<pre><code>public int removePlayers(int squadSize, Player[] players) {
    System.out.println(&quot;Who would you like to remove?&quot;);
    String removal = input.nextLine();

    int removalId = -1;
    for (int i = 0; i &lt; squadSize; i++) {
        if (players[i].name.equals(removal)) {
            removalId = i;
            break;
        }
    }
    if (removalId == -1) return squadSize;   // not found

    for (int i = removalId; i &lt; squadSize - 1; i++) {
        players[i] = players[i + 1];
    }
    players[squadSize - 1] = null;

    return squadSize - 1;
}
</code></pre>
<p>Call it as <code>squadSize = removePlayers(squadSize, players);.</code></p>

